OL,4,CFirst minister 'gobsmacked' by         
OL,5,CBurnham's devolution calls rejection   
OL,6,GWales' First Minister Rhun ap Iorwerth 
OL,7,Ghas declared he is "gobsmacked" after  
OL,8,Gcalls for powers to be handed from     
OL,9,GWestminster to Cardiff were snubbed.   
OL,11,FIn a letter to ap Iorwerth, Prime      
OL,12,FMinister Andy Burnham said he was "not 
OL,13,Fpersuaded" by the case to devolve      
OL,14,Fresponsibilities over policing and     
OL,15,Fjustice, the Crown Estate and rail     
OL,16,Finfrastructure to Wales.               
OL,18,FThe first minister told BBC Radio      
OL,19,FWales breakfast that "this is about    
OL,20,FWestminster saying, we decide, it      
OL,21,Fdoesn't matter what the people of      
OL,22,FWales think".                     G2/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
